W("Reference to context: 'She wished to hurry away in order not to be noticed by the other women who were wrapping themselves in rich furs.' (i) What was she wearing? (ii) Why did she hurry? (iii) What does this show?", 3, "(i) Modest, poor wraps that her husband had carried, which clashed with the elegant costume. (1) (ii) She was ashamed of her poverty. (1) (iii) Her vanity and obsession with appearances. (1)", "M"),
W("Reference to context: 'How singular is life, and how full of changes! How small a thing will ruin or save one!' (i) Who thinks this? (ii) When? (iii) What does it mean?", 3, "(i) Matilda. (1) (ii) Years later, as she sits by the window remembering the ball. (1) (iii) A small event, such as the loss of a necklace, can change a whole life for better or worse. (1)", "M"),
W("Describe the Loisels' life of hardship for ten years in four points.", 3, "They sent away the maid and moved to an attic. Matilda did all housework: washing dishes and linen and carrying water, haggling over every sou. Loisel worked evenings keeping merchants' books and copying at five sous a page. They repaid every debt in ten years. (3)", "M"),
W("How did Matilda change in ten years? Give three details.", 3, "She seemed old, a strong, hard woman, her hair badly dressed and skirts awry, her hands red; she spoke loudly and washed floors with large pails. (3)", "M"),
W("Why did Matilda not tell Mme Forestier the truth at once?", 3, "She was afraid that Mme Forestier would think her a thief or that the loss would shame her; Loisel suggested saying that the clasp was broken to gain time. They then decided to replace the necklace secretly. (3)", "M"),
W("Vocabulary in context: Explain 'incessantly' in 'She suffered incessantly' and give a synonym.", 2, "'Incessantly' means continuously, without stopping. Synonym: constantly. (2)", "M"),
W("Vocabulary in context: Match: (a) tureen (b) usurers (c) awry (d) ruinous with (1) money-lenders at high interest (2) twisted, not in correct position (3) disastrous (4) covered dish for serving soup.", 2, "(a)-(4), (b)-(1), (c)-(2), (d)-(3). (all correct = 2; two or three = 1)", "M"),
W("Vocabulary in context: What does 'frigid' mean in 'said in a frigid tone'? What does it show about Mme Forestier?", 2, "'Frigid' means very cold, not friendly. It shows her displeasure at the delay in returning the necklace, though she was unaware of the loss. (2)", "M"),
