W("Grammar in context: Combine using 'although': She was pretty. She was unhappy.", 2, "Although she was pretty, she was unhappy. (2)", "M"),
W("Character: Write three qualities of Mr Loisel with evidence.", 3, "Kind and generous: he gives the four hundred francs saved for a gun. Loving: he wants her to enjoy the party. Hardworking and honest: he works evenings and nights to pay the debt. (1+1+1)", "M"),
W("Character: Is Matilda a villain or a victim of her own nature? Argue in 40-50 words.", 3, "She is not a villain but a victim of her own vanity. Her discontent and love of show make her borrow jewels and then hide the loss. Her pride, not wickedness, leads to ten years of ruin. She does face hardship bravely, which wins sympathy. (3)", "M"),
